r many  of the teams that you feel like really  like you  uh  yeah i mean a couple of them but like  from like draft drastors i've been here  he's like i'm just like you get by a  team that doesn't eat that hasn't even  really popped into that i mean i'm just  keeping out the door a little bit  you know at six foot seven uh and uh  highly athletic there are other sports  that maybe you could have tried if it  wasn't football what would you be doing  athletically  uh  i mean probably basketball but i just  never had that love for basketball like  i love football so i mean basketball is  fun but it was more like a side sport  you know i played it here and there this  time but football's just always been  that sport for me you know  what sparked that love of football  where'd that come from  i'd say  i said it mattered video game so just  just having that in the house at an  early age really just made me like super  interested in this morning when i got on  the field and started playing it i fell  in love with it even more  you've talked about wanting to improve  in all areas is there one specific area  you you feel like you really need to  improve that to have a great rookie year  i'd definitely say for me just getting  my hands to put this big thing up  well gregory i play a lot of madden even  though i'm old i'm not supposed to i do  and i'm always looking for a good edge  rusher i like using that goal line man  formation where you bring the right side  outside linebacker up to and he gets on  top of the quarterback before the  quarterback and get rid of the ball so  i'm looking forward to getting gregory  rousseau coming off the edge 95 speed  and putting the quarterback on his ass  before he gets gets a chance to throw it  i can't wait for that  it's there use me man use me i gotcha  all right well hey we wish you all the  best congratulations on your success at  the university of miami we look forward  to seeing what happens for you in 17  days nfl draft coming u